## Interactive

### Build a graph, see its score

Choose a direction, or none, for each pair of commute variables. The explorer adds up the graph's Bayesian score from precomputed per-variable terms (@eq-decomposable), on 3,000 simulated mornings with the BDeu prior. It reports how the graph compares with the true one, and whether the two are Markov equivalent. Start from the true graph, then try reversing storm–alert (equivalent, same score), reversing roadwork–jam, or adding extra edges.


